30,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"It seems our most successful projects are those with open booking access, though older blocks hide hazardous materials that cause delays.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,1,talk,Victoria,,My findings confirm a shortage of general-purpose rooms and a high cost for off-site replacements when rooms are closed.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,1,talk,George,,"The grounds staff are depleted, but interestingly, bench technicians are wasting hours on manual tasks the equipment should handle.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"Weather has caused significant delays for outdoor work, and projects based on ""comfort"" tend to slip more than mandatory ones.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Mechanical costs are rising sharply, and we have a funding gap for replacing old audiovisual equipment.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@George, those manual routines you mentioned sound like a failure in equipment design.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Mizuki, if outdoor work is so prone to weather delays, we should be cautious about external projects.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,2,talk,George,,"@Toshio, exactly. The staff are burdened by outdated systems.","{""words"":9,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Victoria, that is a fair point. Internal conversions might be more predictable.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Toshio, if the ""comfort"" projects slip, we must ensure the chosen plan has a clear, mandatory rationale.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
